---
title: Server-side rendering
layout: guide
description: Render Carbon Components Svelte on the server with SvelteKit, avoid theme and layout flashes, and keep generated ids stable.
---

## Basic

Carbon Components Svelte renders on the server without extra setup. Import one stylesheet in your root layout and keep the `optimizeImports` preprocessor from the [quick start](/quick-start).

```svelte
<!-- src/routes/+layout.svelte -->
<script>
  import "carbon-components-svelte/css/white.css";
</script>

<slot />
```

SvelteKit emits the stylesheet as a `<link>` in the document `<head>`, so the first paint is styled. Use `carbon-components-svelte/css/all.css` instead when you need dynamic themes with `Theme`; `white.css`, `g10.css`, `g80.css`, `g90.css`, and `g100.css` each contain a single fixed theme.

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Add `optimizeCss()` from `carbon-preprocess-svelte` to `vite.config.js`. | It prunes the stylesheet to the components you use. A sample app went from 653,132 to 378,489 bytes with `all.css`, and the `[theme]` rules still applied. |

Nothing in the library needs `{#if browser}` to avoid a server error. Every exported component renders on the server without throwing.

## Hydration

Components hydrate in place, and Svelte reports no warnings for them. Most keep every DOM node; generated ids change (see [Stable ids](#stable-ids)) and Svelte 5 rebuilds `<option>` elements, neither of which you can see.

These hydrate with no visible change: Accordion, Breadcrumb, Button, Checkbox, ComboBox without `selectedId`, CopyButton, DataTable without `virtualize` and `stickyHeader`, Dropdown, FileUploader, Form, Link, Menu and Modal when closed, MultiSelect, Notification, NumberInput, PageHeader, RadioButton, Search, Select, Slider, StructuredList, TextArea, TextInput, Tile, TimePicker, Toggle, and every skeleton.

The rest change between the first server paint and the end of hydration.

| Component | Server output | After hydration |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Tabs, TabsVertical | No selected tab, no `aria-controls` or `aria-labelledby`. Panels are hidden on Svelte 5 and all visible on Svelte 3 and 4. | Selected tab and panel appear. Layout shift 0.007 to 0.011. <!-- FIX: SSR-02 #4211 --> |
| ContentSwitcher, ProgressIndicator | Selection and current step missing | Selection and current step appear <!-- FIX: SSR-03 --> |
| Carousel | "Slide 0 of 0", buttons disabled | Real count, active slide <!-- FIX: SSR-04 --> |
| InterstitialScreen with `open` | No progress indicator or footer buttons | Progress and footer appear <!-- FIX: SSR-04 --> |
| ComposedModal | No accessible name on the dialog | `aria-label` set <!-- FIX: SSR-06 #4212 --> |
| Dialog with `open` | Closed | Open <!-- FIX: SSR-08 #4213 --> |
| ComboBox with `selectedId` | Empty input | Item text shown. Pass `value` as well to render it on the server. <!-- FIX: SSR-07 --> |
| Pagination | Page select shows page 1 | Page select shows `page` <!-- FIX: SSR-09 --> |
| TreeView | Nested nodes not indented | Indented <!-- FIX: SSR-10 --> |
| DataTable with `virtualize` and `stickyHeader` | No scroll container height | Scroll container sized <!-- FIX: SSR-11 #4214 --> |
| SideNav and Content | See [Side navigation](#side-navigation) | Content moves, hamburger appears <!-- FIX: SSR-12 --> |
| UserAvatarGroup, TagSet | All items, `+0` | Overflow collapses after measuring <!-- FIX: SSR-05 --> |
| Open `Menu`, tooltips with `portalTooltip`, Portal | Content renders inline at the top left | Moved to the body and positioned <!-- FIX: SSR-14 #4219 --> |
| Breakpoint | The slot sees `size` as `undefined` | The slot sees the real size |
| LocalStorage, SessionStorage | The default value | The stored value |
| CodeSnippet, ScrollGradient, ExpandableTile, open OverflowMenu and Tooltip | Unmeasured state | Measured state |
| ImageLoader | No `<img>` | Image appears after load <!-- FIX: SSR-24 #4216 --> |
| NotificationQueue | Empty by design | Notifications added in `onMount` appear |
| Modal, ComposedModal with `open` | Visible, body scroll not locked | Body gets `bx--body--with-modal-open` |
| ToolbarSearch, DatePicker | Plain input | Text typed before hydration is cleared in ToolbarSearch; DatePicker input loses focus <!-- FIX: SSR-18 SSR-19 --> |

On Svelte 3 and 4 the server writes boolean ARIA attributes without a value (`aria-hidden` instead of `aria-hidden="true"`), so icons are not hidden from assistive technology until hydration. <!-- FIX: SSR-15 -->

Svelte repairs mismatched attributes and text without a warning, so a quiet console does not prove the server and client agree.

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Gate client-only content with a flag set in `onMount`. | The server and the first client render match, so Svelte keeps the nodes. |
| Avoid `{#if browser}` around markup. | `browser` is already `true` during hydration, so the branches differ and Svelte rebuilds the nodes without a warning. |
| Prefer CSS media queries over `Breakpoint` for layout. | The server has no viewport, so `Breakpoint` renders its fallback until mount. |

```svelte
<script>
  import { onMount } from "svelte";
  import { LocalStorage } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  let mounted = false;
  let value = "default";

  onMount(() => (mounted = true));
</script>

<LocalStorage key="draft" bind:value />
<p>{mounted ? value : "Loading"}</p>
```

## Theme without a flash

<!-- FIX: #4183 adds Theme system; the inline script then needs a prefers-color-scheme branch -->

`Theme` writes the `theme` attribute and `color-scheme` on `<html>` only in the browser, when the component initializes, so the server HTML has no `theme` attribute and the first paint uses the default theme. `persist` reads `localStorage` in `onMount`, later still. A saved dark theme therefore paints white first. Set the same attribute from an inline script in `src/app.html` so the first paint already uses it. Replace `"theme"` if you set `persistKey`.

```html
<!-- src/app.html -->
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <script nonce="%sveltekit.nonce%">
      try {
        var raw = localStorage.getItem("theme");
        var theme = raw;
        try {
          theme = JSON.parse(raw);
        } catch (e) {}
        if (/^(white|g10|g80|g90|g100)$/.test(theme)) {
          var root = document.documentElement;
          root.setAttribute("theme", theme);
          root.style.colorScheme =
            theme === "white" || theme === "g10" ? "light" : "dark";
        }
      } catch (e) {}
    </script>
    %sveltekit.head%
  </head>
  <body>
    <div>%sveltekit.body%</div>
  </body>
</html>
```

```svelte
<!-- src/routes/+layout.svelte -->
<script>
  import "carbon-components-svelte/css/all.css";
  import { Theme } from "carbon-components-svelte";

  let theme = "white";
</script>

<Theme bind:theme persist />

<slot />
```

| Do | Why |
| --- | --- |
| Import `all.css`, not `white.css`. | Only `all.css` contains the `[theme="g100"]` rules that the attribute selects. |
| Put the script in `<head>`. | It must run before the first paint. |
| Parse the stored value and fall back to the raw string. | `Theme` stores the bare name (`g100`), so `JSON.parse` alone throws on it. |
| Keep `nonce="%sveltekit.nonce%"` when you set a CSP. | Strict policies block inline scripts without a nonce. |
| For a fixed dark app, set `theme="g100"` on `<html>` in `app.html` and pass the same value to `Theme`. | The attribute is the whole mechanism, so no script is needed. |

Custom `tokens` are applied after hydration, so a theme that relies on them still changes once. <!-- FIX: SSR-21 -->

## Side navigation

On a wide screen the server paints `SideNav` through a CSS media query but without the `bx--side-nav--expanded` class, so `Content` starts under the nav and jumps 208px after hydration. Add these rules to your global CSS. They give the server frame the same margin the hydrated page uses.

```css
/* src/routes/layout.css, imported from +layout.svelte */
@media (min-width: 66rem) {
  .bx--side-nav.bx--side-nav--ux:not(.bx--side-nav--collapsed):not(.bx--side-nav--rail) ~ .bx--content {
    margin-left: 16rem;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 65.99rem) {
  .bx--side-nav.bx--side-nav--ux:not(.bx--side-nav--rail) ~ .bx--content {
    margin-left: 0;
  }
}
```

With these rules the `Content` left edge is 256px on a 1280px screen and 0 on a 400px screen both before and after hydration. <!-- FIX: SSR-12 -->

On a small screen the hamburger button is missing until hydration, so the navigation cannot be opened without JavaScript. <!-- FIX: SSR-12 -->

`SideNav` writes its `resizable` width and `rail` state to module-level stores while rendering, and a later request can read them. Give every route the same `SideNav` props until this is fixed. <!-- FIX: SSR-01 -->

## Stable ids

Most components generate an id with a random value, such as `ccs-8t2995v243o`, for `id`, `for`, `aria-controls`, `aria-labelledby`, and form `name` attributes. The server and the browser draw different values. Svelte rewrites the attributes during hydration and keeps every reference matched, so nothing breaks, but three things follow.

| Effect | Why it matters |
| --- | --- |
| Prerendered HTML differs on every build. | Snapshot tests and cache diffs show noise. |
| A CSS selector, anchor, or script that uses a generated id sees a different value after hydration. | The rewrite is silent. |
| A form submitted without JavaScript posts a random field name. | Applies to `RadioButtonGroup`, `TileGroup`, `StructuredList`, and the `DataTable` selection input when you pass no `name`. |

Pass your own `id`, `name`, or `inputName` to make the markup identical on every render. Ids must be unique on the page, so derive them from the item key inside `{#each}` blocks. In a Svelte 5 component, `$props.id()` gives you a value that matches on the server and the client.

```svelte
<TextInput id="email" labelText="Email" name="email" />
<RadioButtonGroup legendText="Plan" name="plan" id="plan">
  <RadioButton id="plan-free" value="free" labelText="Free" />
  <RadioButton id="plan-pro" value="pro" labelText="Pro" />
</RadioButtonGroup>
<DataTable selectable inputName="orders" {headers} {rows} />
```

| Component | Props that fix its ids |
| --- | --- |
| TextInput, PasswordInput, TextArea, NumberInput, Search, Slider, Toggle, Select, Dropdown, ComboBox, MultiSelect, Modal, OverflowMenu, Pagination, CodeSnippet, CopyInput, Tag, TooltipIcon, TooltipDefinition | `id` |
| Tooltip | `tooltipId` and `triggerId` |
| Tabs | `id` on each `Tab` and `TabContent` |
| ContentSwitcher, ProgressIndicator | `id` on each `Switch` or `ProgressStep` |
| CheckboxGroup, RadioButtonGroup | `id` on the group (helper, error, and warning ids derive from it) |
| RadioButtonGroup, TileGroup | `name` on the group |
| DatePicker | `id` on `DatePicker` and on each `DatePickerInput` |

These components have no prop that fixes every generated id today: Accordion, TreeView, DataTable (table, header, and cell ids), TableContainer, Disclosure, Carousel, ComposedModal, Toggletip, FormGroup (message id), HeaderSearch, ProgressBar and Meter (helper text id), the `Tag` children of TagSet, and StructuredList. <!-- FIX: SSR-20 #4220 #4221 #4222: add `id` to Accordion, Disclosure, Carousel, Toggletip, HeaderSearch, FormGroup, ProgressBar, Meter, TagSet, DataTable, and TableContainer and `name` to StructuredList -->

## Locale and time

`Pagination` and `Meter` format numbers with the runtime locale, so a server in one locale and a browser in another print `12,345` and `12.345`. Svelte replaces the text on hydration. `BigNumber` and `RelativeTime` accept `locale`, and `RelativeTime` accepts `now`; pass fixed values from the request to keep prerendered HTML correct. <!-- FIX: SSR-16 #4224 (Meter locale) SSR-17 #4223 (RelativeTime timeZone) -->
